# How to cite GATOR. GitHub reads this file for its "Cite this repository" button.
# No paper describes GATOR and it has no DOI, so the citation is the repository itself.
# The date is the day the repository became public. The README's "Citing and licence" says the same in words.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GATOR, please cite this repository. No paper describes it."
type: software
title: "GATOR: Graph-Aware Transformer Optimizer for Reinforcement learning"
abstract: >-
  GATOR sizes analog circuits: it searches for the device sizes that make a circuit of fixed topology meet its
  specifications. It proposes sizes by reinforcement learning (Soft Actor-Critic) with a neural network that reads the
  circuit as a graph, and it simulates every proposal in Cadence Spectre or ngspice.
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Fengyan
repository-code: "https://github.com/FengyanWong/gator"
url: "https://github.com/FengyanWong/gator"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-05
